WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:07.099
League of Legends is the most played video
game in the world, which, considering it's

00:00:07.099 --> 00:00:11.120
only been around since 2009 is quite an achievement.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:17.670
League of Legends has over 32 million active
players and 12 million people play on a daily

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:18.700
basis.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:24.720
If you've never played League of Legends before
let me give you a quick rundown.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:35.760
LoL, as it's commonly referred to, is a MOBA
which stands for "Multiplayer Online Battle

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:41.780
Arena", developed by Riot Games, a company
started by a couple of entrepreneurial gamers.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:47.210
MOBA's are a sub-genre of real time strategy
games, based off a custom map for StarCraft

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.190
called Aeon of Strife.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:55.210
There are a handful of popular MOBAs, namely
Defense of the Ancients and Heroes of Newerth.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.690
But none come close to the popularity of LoL.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:05.320
A typical game in a MOBA consists of 2 teams
of 5 players who battle it out on a map containing

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.330
3 lanes.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.850
The goal is to push the 3 lanes all the way
to the enemy base, eventually invading the

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:15.640
enemies' base and destroying their nexus to
win.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.689
Each player chooses a unique champion to play
as.

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:23.619
In League of Legends there are over 100 champions
to choose from, each with their own set of

00:01:23.619 --> 00:01:25.770
attributes and abilities.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.249
Players can gain an advantage over their enemies
by last hitting minions, securing kills and

00:01:31.249 --> 00:01:35.289
assists, and slaying the various monsters
scattered around the map.

00:01:35.289 --> 00:01:40.569
All these give you and your team bonus gold,
which can be spent on better items to make

00:01:40.569 --> 00:01:42.520
your champion stronger.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:48.630
More than 10 new League of Legends games start
every second and the LoL servers regularly

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:52.619
support over 5 million concurrent players
globally.

00:01:52.619 --> 00:01:59.700
To put that in perspective, the top 100 games
on Steam have an average of 650,000 concurrent

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.509
players, all put together.

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:07.289
But the numbers get even more mind blowing:
Every single month, League of Legends players

00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:10.310
play well over 1 billion hours of LoL.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:16.060
That's rather incredible, considering that
since 2004 Halo players have played a cumulative

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.040
2 billion hours.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:25.080
Over 90% of LoL players are male and 85% are
between the ages 16 to 30.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:31.950
Teemo, the ever so annoying Yordle, dies 6.5
million times a day, that's 75 deaths per

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:32.950
second.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:40.930
The chance of you getting a Penta Kill is
just 0.05%, that's only once in every 1,500

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.099
games.

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:47.780
Above Penta Kill, there once was Legendary
Kill, awarded for getting 6 or more kills

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:48.780
in a row.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:53.939
Which is possible if the enemy takes revive
and teleport, but it has since been removed

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:54.959
from the game.

00:02:54.959 --> 00:02:59.410
Riot is constantly adding new easter eggs
to the game, such as:

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:03.790
Your team will lose the game if they surrender
after the enemy has surrendered.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:07.480
There is a cupcake inside Caitlyn's trap.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:12.629
Destroying the enemy nexus grants you 50 gold,
but it's completely useless because the game

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:13.629
is over.

00:03:13.629 --> 00:03:19.530
The in game clock skips from 0:07 to 0:11
every game.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:25.499
Vladamir has been nerfed more than 10 times
since his release, whereas Trundle has never

00:03:25.499 --> 00:03:27.280
been touched.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:32.879
Between 8-10 new champions are in development
by Riot at any given time.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:39.459
Leona's passive "Sunlight" does one less damage
to champions wearing sunglasses, such as Vayne.

00:03:39.459 --> 00:03:44.980
When Fizz uses his ultimate Chum the Waters
if the enemy champion is small, like Annie

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:50.549
and dies from the attack, their body gets
eaten by the shark, instead of leaving a corpse

00:03:50.549 --> 00:03:52.040
on the ground like normal.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:57.319
There are 4 ninjas in the League, Shen, Akali,
Kennen and Zed.

00:03:57.319 --> 00:04:02.569
All of these champions have a special buff
called "Ninja" which reads, "This unit is

00:04:02.569 --> 00:04:04.280
a flippin' ninja!".

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:09.499
Ninjas are more effective on their own, so
for every ninja on your team beyond yourself

00:04:09.499 --> 00:04:11.379
you lose one health.

00:04:11.379 --> 00:04:16.420
Nidalee can turn into a cougar, she has a
hidden passive which grants her the power

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.840
of the "cougar".

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:24.430
This passive grants nearby allied champions
+5 experience every 5 seconds, if they are

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.120
a lower level than Nidalee.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:28.509
Riot is constantly releasing new champions.

00:04:28.509 --> 00:04:34.400
For two years in a row Riot played an April
Fool's Day joke on their players by announcing

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.430
the release of a new champion, Urf, the manatee.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:43.310
The legend of Urf became so popular that Riot
released a new skin for Warwick, Urf the Manatee

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.310
Warwick.

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:49.650
The skin was such a success that Riot decided
to donate the proceeds from the skin to the

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:51.310
Save the Manatee Club.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:56.361
That's about it for easter eggs but here's
some things you might not know about the game

00:04:56.361 --> 00:04:59.139
that might help you out in solo queue:

00:04:59.139 --> 00:05:03.289
Turrets do more damage to champions with each
successive hit.

00:05:03.289 --> 00:05:10.949
Starting at 105%, up to a maximum of 225%
on it's sixth hit and beyond.

00:05:10.949 --> 00:05:16.390
Making a mental note of when buffs such as
Golems, Elder Lizard, Dragon and Baron Nashor

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:21.889
respawn can help you secure the buffs before
your opponents even realise they're there.

00:05:21.889 --> 00:05:27.860
The blue and red buff respawn every 5 minutes,
the dragon every 6 minutes and Baron Nashor

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.770
every 7 minutes.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:33.599
Many champions have auto attack timer resetting
abilities.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:39.610
Meaning you can auto attack, use an ability
then auto attack again in quick succession

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.370
for tons of damage.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:44.640
A good example of this is Vayne's tumble.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:48.310
Most beginners under appreciate the value
of last hitting minions.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:55.389
But perfectly last hitting one minion wave
gives you 124 gold, that means last hitting

00:05:55.389 --> 00:05:58.520
3 minion waves is worth more than a kill.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:02.830
And here's some fundamental tips that will
instantly improve your gameplay:

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:08.449
Maintain constant map awareness, in between
last hits and whenever else you can, you should

00:06:08.449 --> 00:06:09.919
be looking at your mini map.

00:06:09.919 --> 00:06:15.610
If an enemy is missing from the map, there's
a reason for it, they're either dead, jungling

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:17.140
or coming to gank you.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:22.139
A handy tip is to press tab when you see an
enemy missing to bring up the scoreboard,

00:06:22.139 --> 00:06:26.550
this will tell you two things very quickly,
how many enemies are dead and how many are

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:27.819
visible on the map.

00:06:27.819 --> 00:06:29.980
The greyed out champions are MIA.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.990
Play for your team, not yourself.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:38.789
This is one of the major factors that separates
gold players from platinum and diamond players.

00:06:38.789 --> 00:06:45.129
You should have the mindset that everything
you do in game is to aid your team and not

00:06:45.129 --> 00:06:47.819
improve your KDA ratio.

00:06:47.819 --> 00:06:53.750
LoL is a team game and the pros didn't get
where they are today by playing for themselves.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.800
Learn how to counter pick and counter build.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:01.789
Some champions are inherently weak against
others, instantly giving you the upper hand.

00:07:01.789 --> 00:07:07.129
So instead of complaining when the enemy picks
Kassadin, play as Pantheon or Talon mid and

00:07:07.129 --> 00:07:11.639
get an early Null-Magic Mantle, then watch
as you wreck his face.

00:07:11.639 --> 00:07:16.370
This leads me onto my next tip, don't play
a champion you're not good with, just because

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:20.280
you think they're overpowered or counter another
champion.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:25.229
The best way to get good at the game quickly
is to choose one champion and only play that

00:07:25.229 --> 00:07:26.229
champion.

00:07:26.229 --> 00:07:29.669
You're a lot more likely to win a game if
you know your champion back to front than

00:07:29.669 --> 00:07:34.050
if you're playing a supposedly OP champion
you're no good with.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:37.169
Use wards, lots of wards.

00:07:37.169 --> 00:07:41.880
Wards aren't just for supports, every champion
should buy wards throughout the entire the

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:42.880
game.

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:47.110
Don't go mad, but a well placed ward around
your lane or in the enemy jungle will save

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:52.889
your life time and time again and get you
free kills you wouldn't have otherwise got.

00:07:52.889 --> 00:07:57.969
Don't forget objectives such as towers and
dragon, they all give global gold to your

00:07:57.969 --> 00:07:58.969
entire team.

00:07:58.969 --> 00:08:03.509
But learn which objectives are most important
and when you should take them.

00:08:03.509 --> 00:08:09.740
Here is a general tier list of objectives,
from most important to least important: Nexus,

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:18.289
Inhibitors, Baron, Towers, Dragon, Champion
Kills, Buffs and finally smaller jungle camps.

00:08:18.289 --> 00:08:21.610
Constantly find ways to counter the enemy
team's plays.

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:26.910
For example, if the entire enemy are trying
to push bottom and 4 of your teams mates are

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:32.120
defending bottom, solo push top and try and
take a tower.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:39.670
Most likely your team can defend bottom 4
vs 5 and your team got a free tower.

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:45.180
If the enemy send more than one person top
to kill you, then simply recall, you've wasted

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:48.780
the enemy team's time which is a big advantage
in itself.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:51.830
Has the enemy mid laner gone to gank top?

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:56.840
Try to take the middle tower whilst they're
away, towers are worth a lot more than a kill.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:00.920
But don't forget to warn your top lane that's
there's a gank incoming.

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:04.890
But League of Legends isn't just for fun,
it's serious business.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:10.900
eSports is one of the fastest growing sports
and LoL has overtaken Starcraft as the world's

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:12.240
biggest eSport.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:20.090
The 2013 League of Legends World Championship
drew in an astonishing 18 million unique viewers.

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:23.860
Which is more than a lot of traditional televised
sports.

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:30.730
Riot Games offered a handsome $2 million prize
pool which 14 of the world's best teams competed

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:31.940
for a share of.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:40.120
Eight thousand fans showed up to cheer for
their favourite team at the live event, which

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:45.940
was also broadcast all over the world via
the internet and on national TV in South Korea,

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:51.080
where eSports is taken very seriously by the
majority of the population.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:55.370
When asked, many League of Legends players
reported that they actually prefer watching

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:58.750
professionals play than playing themselves.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:04.670
It is rumoured that eSports could become an
olympic sport, as soon as 2020.

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:10.500
League of Legends as a competitive sport is
making a big splash in North America and Europe.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:13.700
Pro gaming houses are popping up all over
the world.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:18.420
A gaming house is a special house where a
professional team and their management lives

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:23.750
permanently so they can practice together
around the clock, it may shock people that

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:26.790
so much time and money is put into professional
gaming.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:32.010
But nothing compares to the game's impact
in South Korea, where eSports is nothing short

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.080
of a cultural phenomenon.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:38.971
Professional teams in South Korea are backed
by multi-billion dollar sponsors, professional

00:10:38.971 --> 00:10:44.950
League of Legends can earn close to 1 million
dollars a year, that's more than some premiership

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:46.890
football players in the UK.

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:52.760
But playing at that level requires over 8
hours of practice every day to stay at tournament

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:53.800
level.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:58.360
Korean teams are strictly controlled by their
management to ensure they get the best out

00:10:58.360 --> 00:10:59.620
of their players.

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:05.420
Players must wake up early, workout at the
gym daily and go to bed at specific times.

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:10.370
Teams also have a handful of player coaches,
as well as nutritionists and personal chefs

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.301
to ensure they are eating a balanced diet.

00:11:12.301 --> 00:11:18.300
It's an awful lot of dedication but for many
people playing games for a living is a dream

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:19.300
come true.

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:22.320
Thanks for the view, subscribe for more Thoughty2.

